[[SECTION]]
MID: eb0685f50def4479b361cc475d4bd795
TITLE: Project config

[[SECTION]]
MID: 17ee741a300748f2989cd85d0638906c
TITLE: ProjectConfig

[REQUIREMENT]
MID: 50d648852d7b4dafa2a3b87779d11f7e
UID: SDOC-LLR-209
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Config rule for custom node prefix
STATEMENT: >>>
The ProjectConfig shall provide an argument/property that allows a user to
define a custom Python function where a custom node prefix can be defined for
the following combination of inputs: (node, grammar_element, document,
traceability_index, project_config).

The return value of the function shall be a prefix string.

A user shall be able to optionally revert to the default behavior in the
function implementation. Example:

.. code-block:: py

    def custom_node_prefix(
        node,
        grammar_element,
        document,
        traceability_index,
        project_config
    ):
        if document.reserved_uid == "MY_UID":
            return "MY_UID_PREFIX"
        # Default prefix.
        return None
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
MID: 6a1cf6b5efc84fdca6a0ff5cc3f52f0c
UID: SDOC-LLR-210
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Config rule for custom node UID
STATEMENT: >>>
The ProjectConfig shall provide an argument/property that allows a user to
define a custom Python function where a node's full UID can be composed from
its resolved prefix and next available number, for the following combination
of inputs: (prefix, next_number, node, grammar_element, document,
traceability_index, project_config).

The return value of the function shall be a UID string.

A user shall be able to optionally revert to the default behavior
(``f"{prefix}{next_number}"``) in the function implementation. Example:

.. code-block:: py

    def custom_node_uid(
        prefix,
        next_number,
        node,
        grammar_element,
        document,
        traceability_index,
        project_config
    ):
        if document.reserved_uid == "MY_UID":
            return f"{prefix}{next_number:04d}"
        # Default UID.
        return None
<<<

